!! Proposed Definition of ''ga'i''

;__ga'i__ (UI5): hauteur.  This word is an attitudinal, that is, it directly expresses an emotion on the part of the speaker.  This word is part of a scale; the base attitudinal word indicates that the speaker is feeling hauteur, the base word followed by cu'i indicates that the speaker is feeling equal rank, and the base word followed by nai indicates that the speaker is feeling meekness; used with one of lower rank.(cf. gapru, cnita)
